{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LEAF 9ca8 — phases 4a-4d.\n\n4b RED-FIRST, 28 tests (6 visible + 22 held out) against an inert skeleton. Result 22 FAILED / 6\npassed, all right-reason: KeyError 'config_key' (no detection), 'a new <kind> slipped through' x7\n(the core, one per kind), marker not named in the failure, blank reason not rejected x2, marker\nover-admits its whole kind, removal not bucketed stale, --update-stale does not refuse, baseline file\nabsent, make lint not wired, docs name no kind.\n\nMY OWN GUARD CAUGHT MY OWN NEW TEST, correctly: the AC16 complexity check spawns ruff with\ncwd=REPO_ROOT, which is a genuine hazard by the rule, and it genuinely needs the real checkout (it\nlints the SHIPPED files). Added the opt-out marker with a reason. Good validation that 2506's guard\nfires on brand-new code, not just on the tree it was written against.\n\nORACLE ENCODES THE R4 LESSON: a test asserts that every REPEATED config key produces one entry PER\nSECTION. Live tree has TWO such collisions, not the one the reviewer named — allow_insecure\n(reconciler + jira) AND threshold (ticket_clarity + compact) — so a bare-key baseline would silently\nmerge FOUR definition sites into TWO entries.\n\nLIVE COUNTS VERIFIED FOR THE BASELINE: 16 sections / 103 keys = 27 boolean (feature_flag) + 76\n(config_key); check_*.py now 30 and tests/_*.py now 20 — both up by one because THIS EPIC added a\ngate script and a test helper. That is correct and intended: the epic said the ratchet is the bound\nfor its own additions, so the baseline locks against the tree including them.\n\n4d DISPATCHED with the partition rule, the section-qualification requirement, the per-detection-shape\nmarker table, the gen_env_registry union caveat (scan() misses the deprecation-alias and MCP-derived\nenv families), the import-walk constraint that forces a subpackage, and an EXPLICIT instruction to\nrun tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py and add the synthetic-repo stub — the exact step\nwhose omission CI caught on 2503. Also warned it about the concurrent parity edits in this worktree."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788322826790380001,"uuid":"b51b28d8-c63b-4f42-9fba-768d1af067a9"}